From: xxlloydzz <xxlloydzz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topaz-0952: TopazModem: restore <sys/vnode.h> for 0951

Companion to 0951. The root-vnode wait in topaz_soc_map() uses
vfs_rootvnode(), vnode_put() and NULLVP, which live in <sys/vnode.h>.
Patch 0113 included that header, but 0115 removed it (along with the
vnode-based firmware file reads) when firmware loading moved to the
modem_a partition, so 0951 no longer compiles:

  TopazModem.cpp: error: use of undeclared identifier 'vfs_rootvnode'
  TopazModem.cpp: error: use of undeclared identifier 'NULLVP'
  TopazModem.cpp: error: use of undeclared identifier 'vnode_put'

Put the include back. Nothing else changes.

---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,8 @@
 #include <kern/thread.h>
 #include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
 #include <libkern/crc.h>
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/errno.h>
+#include <sys/vnode.h>
 
 extern "C" vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t phys_addr, vm_size_t size);
